1	// TEMPORARY, local preview only: phase 5 options for the ending, at the top of the Options panel. Once the user
2	// picks, write the chosen words into index.html and the chosen look into styles.css, then delete this file, its
3	// <script> tag and the phase 5 TRYOUT part of styles.css (and endAt/placeEnding in main.js if "After the book" wins).
4	//
5	// Words from agent-skills:idea-refine, 2026-09-13. Who they're for: adults starting from zero, reverts, and parents
6	// choosing for a child, who have just watched the book open on aayat they may not be able to read yet. Each line
7	// comes at it differently: that moment (these pages), reassurance (every reader began with Alif), the two buttons
8	// spelled out, and the whole path from reading to Hifz. Left out: what the subline candidates already say (a real
9	// teacher, one letter at a time, one to one, every age), a free first lesson (not decided), countries, and anything
10	// close to the wording of the aayat. No button says "book", because how lessons get arranged isn't decided either.
11	//
12	// Second round (the user found the ending "dry", with not enough to see): what sits behind the words (nothing, a warm
13	// light, or the light with a large slowly turning gold star) and a name at the very end, both from
14	// taste-skill:minimalist-skill's advice against empty, flat sections. main.js adds "Scroll once it opens" above these.
15	//
16	// Third round: the user wants to type the words themselves, not only choose from presets — see wordmark-options.js
17	// for why. Every preset list here now sits beside a text field bound to the same element, so clicking a preset fills
18	// the field in and the field always shows what the page currently says.
